From cd2432e79d566cfe5e96d1fc5e0a752708af4e17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:05:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(icons): import PNG/JPEG icons and keep embedded
 raster images

Icons are stored and served as SVG everywhere, and _sanitize_svg
removed every data: URI from href/xlink:href. That also dropped the
bitmap of SVGs that embed one (e.g. a photo placed in Inkscape), so
such files imported as an empty ~1 KB icon, and there was no way to
use an icon that only exists as a picture.

Sanitizer (backend and the Visu's useIcons): keep href/xlink:href when
it is a base64 data URI of image/png, image/jpeg, image/gif or
image/webp and the element is <image>. data:image/svg+xml, non-base64
payloads, javascript: and data URIs on any other element (a, use,
feImage, ...) are still removed. A raster image cannot run script, so
the Admin GUI's inline v-html rendering of the icon grid stays safe.

Import: a single upload or ZIP member whose content starts with the PNG
or JPEG signature is wrapped into a minimal SVG
  <svg width=W height=H viewBox="0 0 W H"><image ... href="data:..."/></svg>
with W/H read from the PNG IHDR chunk or the JPEG SOF segment (struct,
no new dependency). Detection is by content as for SVGs; ZIP members
with .png/.jpg/.jpeg are now considered. A raster image may be at most
1 MB (the icon list inlines every icon) and 16384 px per side; an
oversized or unreadable image is rejected with 422, which keeps a ZIP
import atomic like a broken SVG does. The wrapper goes through the same
sanitizer before it is stored.

Admin GUI: the file picker accepts .png/.jpg/.jpeg, the import texts
name the new formats, and the hardcoded upload error fallback is now
translated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
